+# CVE-2026-119123 — Not affected (Debian bookworm)
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| **CVE ID** | CVE-2026-119123 |
+| **Component** | imagemagick (`coders/tiff.c`) |
+| **Distribution** | Debian 12 (bookworm) |
+| **Package version** | `8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u15` |
+| **Upstream affected** | ImageMagick 7.1.2-33 only; fixed in 7.1.2-34 |
+| **Assessment** | **NOT AFFECTED — vulnerable code never landed in this release.** |
+
+CVE-2026-119123 is uncontrolled recursion (CWE-674) in the TIFF reader.
+ImageMagick 7.1.2-33 falls back from `ReadTIFFImage` into the DNG decoder
+through `ReadTIFFImageInternal` and `TIFFTAG_DNGVERSION`. When the DNG
+decoder is disabled, that fallback recurses. ImageMagick 7.1.2-34
+(commit `5f6b60f2e18aa760aae94f0601a2758d190451c8`) returns early when
+`GetMagickInfo("DNG")` is NULL.
+
+Debian bookworm ships ImageMagick 6.9.11-60. `coders/tiff.c` has a single
+`ReadTIFFImage`. It does not contain `ReadTIFFImageInternal`, the
+DNGVersion tag check, or the disabled-DNG fallback. The `deb12u15` quilt
+series does not add them. Cherry-picking `5f6b60f2` has no attachment
+point (`patch -p1` fails). The XMP `dc:format="image/dng"` label in
+`TIFFGetProfiles` does not call `ReadImage`.
+
+The Debian tracker still lists bookworm as vulnerable because the only
+recorded fix is `8:7.1.2.34+dfsg1-1`. That status is the untriaged
+default. Classify this package as **not affected**
+(`vulnerable_code_not_present`).
+
