Description: CVE-2026-123273 - reject zero-sized pixel regions in
 QueueAuthenticPixelCacheNexus() (infinite loop / DoS in the SVG decoder).
 .
 QueueAuthenticPixelCacheNexus() in magick/cache.c validated the starting
 (x,y) coordinate against the cache geometry but never validated the requested
 region size. A crafted SVG image can make the decoder repeatedly request a
 non-advancing (zero width or zero height) pixel region, so the caller never
 makes progress and the decoding worker spins at 100% CPU. Reject requests
 where columns or rows is zero, as the function already does for invalid
 coordinates, so the caller gets a NULL pixel pointer and a "PixelsAreNotAuthentic"
 exception instead of looping.
 .
 Upstream fixed this in ImageMagick6 6.9.13-60 (ImageMagick 7.1.2-35) with
 four commits: 712e523e added a larger bounds check, 1180eb83 fixed its build,
 f1e67cfb reverted that check, and dd2b0729 landed the final fix. Only the
 final commit changes the resulting code, so only dd2b0729 is applied here.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/dd2b0729f6839218474e91ab08bed8ecd33ebabe
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-q66g-3m63-78mh
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1153341
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
Forwarded: not-needed
